{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And the blood he poured upon the base of the altar.</b> To make atonement for the soul of man, whose existence is in the blood, for so it is written (Leviticus 17): ״כי נפש כל בשר דמו בנפשו הוא״, and it is written (ibid.): ״כי הדם הוא בנפש יכפר״. And therefore he would offer up these three things — the fat, the kidneys, and the appendage of the liver — because all three of them collude in sin and incline the people from the good way to the evil way. And this is what is said: <b>and the fat, and the kidneys, and the appendage from the liver, from the sin offering, he offered up upon the altar.</b> The fat is the suet that brings a person to coarseness of spirit, and it is the cause that a person's nature becomes coarse and arrogant, as it says (Deuteronomy 32): ״וישמן ישרון ויבעט שמנת עבית כשית ויטוש וגו׳״, and it is written (Job 15): ״כי כסה פניו בחלבו״. The kidneys are the source of counsel, as they said: the kidneys counsel; (Psalms 16): ״צרפה כליותי ולבי״; (ibid. 16): ״אף לילות יסרוני כליותי״. <b>The liver</b> — from there comes the desiring soul that spreads through a person, and it is what produces anger and wrath and seeks dominion and bodily pleasures. And all this he would offer up on the north side, for from there evil opens forth; and all of it comes to atone for the sin of man that issues from the fat of the heart, and the thought of the heart, and the desire of the liver."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {0 "The second Psalms citation is given as (שם ט״ז), i.e., ibid. to the first citation which is תהלים ס״ו; the verse אף לילות יסרוני כליותי is Psalm 16:7, so the reference appears corrupt — possibly the first should be ט״ז (16) rather than ס״ו (66). Both rendered as printed; the verse צרפה כליותי ולבי is Psalm 26:2."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:24.720995272Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}